// Brandl_14_2_531             We know of these disappearances. Little happens in Prague without our knowledge.

// Ecat_14_2_532               How now? Hast thou discovered the culprit?
// Brandl_14_2_533             We can direct thee aright. Should we feel so moved.
// Ecat_14_2_545               I cannot imagine such a thing as can move thy lordship.
// Brandl_14_2_534             We desire a reliquary containing the arm of Saint George, which lieth in the antechamber of the cathedral of St. Vitus. Alas, a ring of hallowed ground outside the cathedral doth repel Cainites. The sanctified ground extends not into the cathedral, 
// Cosmas_14_2_535             Then how may WE cross the sanctified ring to enter the cathedral?
// Brandl_14_2_536             We tire of thee. Pray do not return until thou hast the arm.
// Ecat_14_2_537               Very well. We go.
// Christof_14_2_539           Nay! To withhold such knowledge is wicked! We seek to save many! Has the Prince no pity, no humanity, that he only bestows his knowledge for a price?
